WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:07.460
<i>Can't you see that you are sweet?</i>

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:15.050
<i>Oh, let me love you so.</i>

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.460
War in the Pocket

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>As I look up, the sky above seems so far away...</i>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>miageru sora wa tooi kedo</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>...but there are dreams that even it can't hold.</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>kakae kirenai yume ga aru</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>Oh, yes, I want to slip away from this artificial world...</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>sou yo, tsukurareta sekai no naka wo mukidashite</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>...and make myself free.</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>jiyuu ni naritai</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>I can keep on running till I finally reach the sky.</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>hashi ni tsuzukete sora ni todoteba</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>Since I can believe that I can become the wind someday...</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>kaze ni nareru to sou shinjiteru kara</i>

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:23.450
<i>I never give up forever.</i>

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.780
Al, can you hear me?

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.530
<i>Loud and clear!</i>

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.160
I'm turning it on now.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.910
<i>Okay.</i>

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.450
Any change on the monitor?

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:59.200
<i>Nothing.</i>

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.790
How about now?

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.630
<i>I just got a display!</i>
D-14 is blinking.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.040
<i>How about on the</i> <i>right-hand monitor?</i>

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.170
A-15 is lit up.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.260
<i>I see...</i>

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.420
Can you fix it?

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:13.420
<i>Of course.</i>

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.720
Can you beat the Gundam?

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.470
<i>Piece of cake!</i>

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.830
War in the Pocket

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.870
We need three things: tools, parts for the Zaku, and weapons.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.660
We can buy the tools.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.000
How about the parts?

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.040
Steal them.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.380
You're gonna be a robber?

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.170
There are wrecked GMs lying all over the colony.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:45.210
I'll salvage the parts from them.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.090
It's just like a treasure hunt.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.390
We could get caught by the Feddies, you know.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:52.180
My mind's made up.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.140
Well said. All right then, let's get some weapons.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.770
There are still two weapons trailers left.
A little gift from Misha.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.910
The Feddies are taking them!

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.290
There's still one left at the parking lot. Let's hurry a little.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.710
That trailer's been parked here for about 3 days.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.670
You're welcome to check it out.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:30.390
Just don't scratch it, okay? I'm responsible for these things.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:31.680
Right, right.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:42.110
The license plates match the rental agency's records.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.020
I'll check the parking meter.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.610
Bernie, I've got a great idea.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.160
The meter says it's been here for three days.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.120
Okay, let's take a look inside.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.250
Get off our colony, you lousy Feds!

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.370
- Hey, kid! What are you doing?!
- Cut that out!

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.380
Get off!

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:02.920
Stop that!

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:03.790
Hey, cut it out!

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:05.170
Stop it! Knock it off!

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.550
Give me my dad back!

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:11.220
What are you talking about?

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.930
You guys killed my dad!

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.970
It's all because you Feds built a base here!

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:24.150
That battle happened, and my dad...

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.780
Give me my dad back...

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:36.490
Now, kid, we know how you feel, but it's all the Zeons' fault.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:39.290
Don't do this again, okay?

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:56.300
One heat hawk and 12 hand grenades. We hit it big!

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:58.970
Great job, Al.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:05.020
Now, let's ditch this trailer and get a new car.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.320
Bernie?

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.660
Whatcha thinking about?

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.660
I don't have enough weapons.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:23.620
Without a rifle, I'll get shot up before I can get close to the Gundam.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:25.080
Can't you steal one?

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.130
That'd be too hard.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:31.550
If only there was some way to do it...

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:37.760
That's it!

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.970
Do you have a good idea?

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.180
Oh, and how!

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.230
Tell me!

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:46.940
Here we go.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.580
- You didn't kill him, did you?
- I just knocked him out.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:18.260
We'll set a trap using the balloons and smoke dischargers.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.600
I think the place should be the forest near the Feddie base.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:23.680
Why?

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:26.390
No civilians to worry about if we fight over there.

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:27.600
Yeah, right!

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.110
<i>Well, then what?</i>

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:35.860
<i>Then I'll draw the Gundam out</i> <i>and ambush him in the forest.</i>

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:39.280
<i>If I do that, I can beat him</i> <i>with just that heat hawk.</i>

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.410
<i>Like I said, a piece of cake.</i>

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:53.460
<i>Can't you see that you are sweet?</i>

00:06:53.500 --> 00:07:00.970
<i>Oh, let me love you so.</i>

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:16.150
<i>As I look up, the sky above seems so far away...</i>

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:23.160
<i>...but there are dreams that even it can't hold.</i>

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:34.000
<i>Oh, yes, I want to slip away from this artificial world...</i>

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:38.380
<i>...and make myself free.</i>

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:52.360
<i>I can keep on running till l finally reach the sky.</i>

00:07:52.560 --> 00:08:02.870
<i>Since I can believe that I can become the wind someday...</i>

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:07.120
<i>I never give up forever.</i>

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:19.050
<i>People may accept those who come to them...</i>

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:24.850
<i>...and may stand there silently, but still...</i>

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:33.270
<i>Oh, yes, I want to know who my true love will be...</i>

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:39.990
<i>...even though I haven't met them yet.</i>

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:47.200
<i>When you reach out your arms far...</i>

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:53.830
<i>...till they finally reach the sky...</i>

00:08:54.380 --> 00:09:04.680
<i>...you can see a new beginning then, and...</i>

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:10.310
<i>You never give up forever.</i>

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:20.740
Don't look so sad. Your dad's coming home tomorrow, right?

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.780
But I won't get to help you fight...

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:28.660
You're sure I can't do anything else to help?

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:30.660
I can handle the fighting by myself.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:37.080
Your job tomorrow is this. I want you to deliver it.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.460
Deliver it where?

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.550
I left instructions on the disk.

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:45.680
If the plan fails... If I die...

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:49.350
Play the disk and do what I tell you to.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:52.770
This is important, Al. I'm counting on you.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.850
If you die?

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:59.360
Just in case. You probably won't need to use it.

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:05.320
Tomorrow at 2:00, I'll destroy the Gundam and save this colony.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.660
Merry Christmas, Al.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.620
You, too, Bernie.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:12.830
Goodnight.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.590
Bernie, you won't die, right? You'll win, right?

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:28.220
Of course I will! Trust me. Now go.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.680
Goodnight, Bernie.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:59.880
<i>God, please give</i> <i>me this one thing.</i>

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:02.920
<i>I swear I won't</i> <i>pull pranks anymore.</i>

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:05.760
<i>I mean it! I promise!</i>

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:08.430
<i>I won't kill frogs</i> <i>for fun anymore.</i>

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:11.890
<i>I won't put snakes and</i> <i>lizards in the girls' desks.</i>

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:15.220
<i>So, please,</i> <i>you've gotta do this.</i>

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:20.980
<i>Protect Bernie. Protect this colony.</i> <i>Don't let everyone here die.</i>

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:23.980
<i>Amen.</i>

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:54.220
<i>NTW flight 205 is now boarding.</i>

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:58.390
<i>It's almost time for</i> <i>him to go. Bernie...</i>

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:00.770
Hey! Al! Dear!

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:03.730
Sorry I'm so late.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:17.830
There was a battle near our ship.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:18.950
Oh, my.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.750
I could see a Zeon ship get destroyed from my own window.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.080
We were also in danger.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:26.380
One of the Zeon ships that surrendered to the Feds...

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:28.920
...was apparently carrying a nuclear missile.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:32.010
Really? They had nuclear weapons?

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:36.100
As far as the Feds can figure it, they were headed for Riah.

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:39.020
But why would they attack a neutral colony?

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:41.940
Al, what's wrong?

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:43.810
Al, this isn't our stop!

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:54.110
<i>He doesn't have to fight now!</i> <i>I have to stop him!</i>

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.580
What?!

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:06.340
Zaku approaching the base. ETA: Three minutes!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.380
What's the Alex have left for armament?

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:10.630
Just five hundred rounds in the right arm.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:14.130
The Riah Forces are saying they're keeping out of this one.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.390
<i>Lieutenant Mackenzie, move out!</i>

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:22.690
Roger!

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:41.700
There it is.

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.510
Come on! Aren't you going to follow me?

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:57.680
Okay. Good boy.

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:03.730
Both units are headed for the foothills.

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:05.690
Lieutenant Mackenzie, pull back!

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:08.230
<i>You have the advantage</i> <i>on flat ground!</i>

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:10.070
There's no one living in the foothills, sir.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:11.150
<i>What?!</i>

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:12.440
I'll fight it in the forest.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:14.070
<i>Lieutenant! Pull back!</i>

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:39.720
Bernie!

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:49.770
Bernie!

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:00.160
Bernie, get out of here!

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:06.710
What the?!

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:28.520
Stop it, please!

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.950
Bernie!

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.140
Bernie!

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:06.890
You don't have to fight now!

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:37.590
Bernie!

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:26.350
How's Lieutenant Mackenzie?!

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:29.180
Alive. Just unconscious.

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:31.270
What about the Zaku pilot?

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:34.560
Nothing left, sir. A pile of hamburger.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:41.030
Hey, kid, you okay? What are you doing here?

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.660
Hey, you all right?

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:53.080
Get a stretcher! Hurry!

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:08.010
Hey! You okay? Hey!

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.350
Come on, kid, snap out of it! Hey!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:31.160
Al... Okay, listen carefully.

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:38.000
Inside the package you'll find a taped confession and evidence.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.000
I included everything I could think of to explain...

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:44.050
...why this colony's been targeted for nuclear attack.

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:48.840
If I die, I want you to take it to the police.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:51.100
If you can get an adult to believe you...

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:53.520
...then they can still save this colony.

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:58.020
I could have taken it to them myself, but...

00:18:58.060 --> 00:19:02.650
Oh, how can I put this? It would've been like running away.

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:05.030
If I ducked out of fighting now...

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:07.610
...I don't think I could live with myself.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:11.530
It's not like I hate the Federation...

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:14.450
...or want to avenge the captain and the others.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:21.420
I'm not sure how to put it, but I <i>want</i> to fight the Gundam now.

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:26.420
Maybe it's because I'm a soldier. I don't really know the reason.

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:31.930
Al, I'm probably going to die. But, whatever happens...

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:36.100
...don't hate the Gundam pilot or the other Feddie soldiers.

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:40.100
Because they're like me.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.440
Just people doing what they think is right.

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:47.190
Maybe I'm asking too much, but don't hate them.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:49.950
And don't blame yourself, either.

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:52.490
Please, this is my last request.

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:59.120
And, if I do manage to get out of this alive and the war ends...

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:04.000
...I'll come back to this colony and visit you.

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:06.670
That's a promise!

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:09.670
Well, I guess that's it.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:12.590
See you, Al. Take care of yourself.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.640
And say hi to Chris for me.

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:30.820
Al? Al!

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:35.370
What's wrong? You were yelling in your sleep.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:38.660
I was dreaming...

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:45.340
What time is it?

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:47.710
About 8:30.

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:53.470
Mm... It's beautiful out today.

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:56.300
It's like God's blessing your first day back to school.

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:15.410
Dear, I can't find a towel anywhere.

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:19.660
Are you trying to get water all over the kitchen?!

00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:21.080
Just a sec.

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:22.620
Dear, what are you?!

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:25.380
Oh, for heaven's sake.

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:36.180
Better get going, Al. You'll be late.

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:37.220
Right.

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:39.140
Do you have your handkerchief?

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:40.180
Got it.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:48.190
Bye.

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:53.900
Does he seem more mature to you? He's so quiet now.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:57.780
Al!

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:07.670
I'm glad I caught you.

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:11.380
I've been transferred back to Earth.

00:22:13.340 --> 00:22:15.090
You're leaving?

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:20.640
I wanted to say goodbye to you properly.

00:22:20.680 --> 00:22:22.970
I hope this isn't a shock for you.

00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:30.190
I wanted to say goodbye to Bernie, too.

00:22:30.230 --> 00:22:32.320
Will you do it for me?

00:22:32.360 --> 00:22:35.110
Just tell him I said hi.

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:40.580
Yeah, Bernie'll...

00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:44.790
Bernie'll be sorry he missed you.

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:49.460
Al?

00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:04.890
Goodbye, Al.

00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:06.940
Goodbye, Chris.

00:23:10.810 --> 00:23:14.400
<i>The long, terrible war is over.</i>

00:23:14.480 --> 00:23:16.820
<i>And peace has</i> <i>finally been restored.</i>

00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:23.330
<i>But this colony, too, carries</i> <i>deep wounds from the war.</i>

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:28.870
<i>Not only have</i> <i>we lost our school.</i>

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:34.300
<i>We've lost countless parents,</i> <i>brothers, sisters, and friends.</i>

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:40.300
<i>This peace was won at the cost</i> <i>of many peoples' lives.</i>

00:23:41.510 --> 00:23:45.600
<i>I hope you all will</i> <i>never forget that.</i>

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:48.560
<i>And when you all grow up...</i>

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:50.520
Al, is something wrong? <i>And when you all grow up...</i>

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:50.980
Al, is something wrong? <i>... I sincerely pray you all...</i>

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:52.520
<i>... I sincerely pray you all...</i>

00:23:52.520 --> 00:23:54.190
<i>... will work hard to make...</i>

00:23:54.190 --> 00:23:56.360
Hold on, I'll get the teacher! <i>... will work hard to make...</i>

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:58.490
<i>... a peaceful world where</i> <i>war will never happen again.</i>

00:23:58.530 --> 00:24:00.240
<i>That is our duty as those</i> <i>who were left behind.</i>

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:04.200
Al, don't cry. Come on, another war'll start soon...

00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:09.000
...and it'll be even bigger, flashier, and more fun than this one!

00:24:09.790 --> 00:24:14.750
Yeah, and maybe we can find some live bullets, not just empty shells.

00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:17.670
And a soldier might even give us his rations, too!

00:25:42.520 --> 00:25:48.300
<i>On that night I told them that lie...</i>

00:25:42.520 --> 00:25:48.300
<i>uso wo tsuita yoru ni wa</i>

00:25:48.890 --> 00:25:55.030
<i>...I couldn't sleep. That's how scared I was.</i>

00:25:48.890 --> 00:25:55.030
<i>nemurezu ni kowakatta</i>

00:25:55.360 --> 00:26:01.440
<i>But no matter how bad of a fight we would have...</i>

00:25:55.360 --> 00:26:01.440
<i>donna kenka wo shite mo</i>

00:26:01.740 --> 00:26:08.310
<i>...by the next day, it would be forgotten.</i>

00:26:01.740 --> 00:26:08.310
<i>tsugi no hi wa wasureteita</i>

00:26:10.610 --> 00:26:15.790
<i>The sky would be so blue...</i>

00:26:10.610 --> 00:26:15.790
<i>sora ga aoi koto</i>

00:26:17.050 --> 00:26:23.130
<i>...and that would make me so glad.</i>

00:26:17.050 --> 00:26:23.130
<i>sore ga ureshikute</i>

00:26:23.760 --> 00:26:29.640
<i>There would be times when I'd doubt others...</i>

00:26:23.760 --> 00:26:29.640
<i>itsuka hito wo utagai</i>

00:26:30.260 --> 00:26:36.580
<i>...and I'd know the loneliness of living.</i>

00:26:30.260 --> 00:26:36.580
<i>itsuka hito wo utagai</i>

00:26:36.640 --> 00:26:42.640
<i>But that was something I didn't notice then.</i>

00:26:36.640 --> 00:26:42.640
<i>ki ga tsukazu ni subete wo</i>

00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:48.080
<i>Back when I believed in everything...</i>

00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:48.080
<i>shinjiteta koro</i>
